From 914c7f719fdcfe87d554282c6dfe2c9f939b74e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:02:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(motion): 2D rest area and rest pocket passes after a
 larger tool

machining2d::rest_plan reads what a larger previous tool could not reach
in a pocket (the pocket minus its opening by the previous tool's disc)
and the cutter-center area that touches it; machining2d::rest_pocket
runs the pocket's ring passes over that area only.

The rest area is read large, never small: the cleared area is shrunk by
a margin, a corner radius and stock left on the walls count as rest
material, the allowance only grows it. The passes are the pocket's own
(plunge and feed below the top of the cut), inside the pocket's own
center area, so a wrong previous tool costs a heavier cut and never a
rapid into stock. Refused by name: a previous tool that is not larger,
Zigzag and Adaptive with rest, nothing left to cut.

pocket.rs: the body of pocket() is pocket_over(), shared with the rest
pass; PocketStrategy moves to pocket_strategy.rs (structure only). The
plain pocket posts as before.

Motion crate only: the operation parameter, its undoable edit, the
project file, the dialog and MCP are follow-up issues.

Refs #1446

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
